  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are twice-differentiable on an open interval containing $x=1.$ The values of $f,$ $g,$ and their respective derivatives are given below:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${f}^{″}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{″}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{f(x)+x}{g(x)-x}.$",
